## Personal Use

Personal use is a permitted purpose.

Personal use is use by an individual, for that individual's own purposes, that is not use by, for
or on behalf of any organization. Personal study, including a student's own learning, your own
research and experiments, hobby projects, private entertainment, amateur pursuits and documenting
your own home network are examples of personal use.

Use is not personal use when it is part of your work for an employer or a client, when it is part
of running a business, including your own business as a sole proprietor, freelancer or
consultant, or when you use the software to produce models, diagrams or other work for an
organization.

## Organizations

Any use of the software by, for or on behalf of an organization needs a written license from the
licensor, whatever kind of organization it is, whether or not it seeks profit, and however it is
funded. Businesses, government institutions at every level, educational institutions, charitable
and other nonprofit organizations, and research organizations all need one. Without a written
license, the only use an organization may make of the software is the evaluation described in
[Evaluation](#evaluation).

The licensor grants written licenses to specific organizations, with or without a fee, at its
discretion. Request one at subscriptions@digitalprez.com; the licensor provides the license
document on request.

## Evaluation

An organization may use the software to evaluate whether it suits the organization's needs for up
to 30 consecutive calendar days, counted from the day the software is first used by, for or on
behalf of that organization. Evaluation within that period is a permitted purpose.

Each organization gets one evaluation period, shared by all of its people and covering every
release of the software, not one period per person, team or release. Evaluation does not include
distributing the software outside the organization. When the evaluation period ends, the
organization must stop using the software unless it holds a written license from the licensor.

## Tools and Service Providers

Running the software with a tool or service that you have chosen, such as an AI assistant, a code
editor or a hosting service, is your use of the software. The provider of that tool or service
needs no license of its own to carry out your instructions. A provider that offers the software,
or a product or service built on it, to others needs a written license from the licensor.

## Output Exception

Diagrams, documents and other files generated with the software, including the copy of the
renderer embedded in them, may be used, copied, displayed and distributed by anyone, for any
purpose, without restriction under these terms. The models and diagrams you make with the
software are yours.

This exception covers the generated files. It is not a license to use the software to generate
them, and it does not allow the embedded renderer to be reused to generate other documents, which
is use of the software.

