## Definitions

The **licensor** is DigitalPrez, LLC, and the **software** is the software the licensor makes
available under these terms.

**You** refers to the individual or organization agreeing to these terms.

An **individual** is one natural person.

An **organization** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship, partnership, association, agency,
institution or other body, whether or not it is incorporated. For counting the evaluation period,
an organization includes every organization that has control over it, is under its control, or is
under common control with it.

**Your organization** is any organization that you work for or act on behalf of, plus all
organizations that have control over, are under the control of, or are under common control with
that organization. **Control** means ownership of substantially all the assets of an entity, or
the power to direct its management and policies by vote, contract, or otherwise. Control can be
direct or indirect.

A **written license** is a license document that the licensor has issued in writing to a named
organization and that covers the use in question.

**Your licenses** are all the licenses granted to you for the software under these terms.

**Use** means anything you do with the software requiring one of your licenses.
